<ecoSpold xmlns="http://www.EcoInvent.org/EcoSpold02">
  <activityDataset>
    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="51fb9284-903d-5473-b7dc-c26ed961f9af" activityNameId="edf061b1-96f0-5bda-ac55-0dc0beb6df59" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Locomotive</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Locomotive
The exchanges of the locomotive manufacturing are derived from an assessment of the RE 460, a locomotive which is currently used for goods transportation in Switzerland and also in Germany. The life span of the locomotive Re 460 is assumed to be 40 years resulting in a life time performance of 9.6 Mio. kilometres. The materials with a weight above 200 kg are accounted for. A detailed specification of electronic components was not possible. Total weight of the locomotive is about 84t.;
UUID: e9f8c142-1372-38e8-b6fd-28e16d130f90
This inventory calls processes of material production, representing the material composition of one locomotive. For manufacturing, electricity and light oil burned in industrial furnance are included. For the transportation of materials standandard distance are applied.
Location: Manufacturing data represents a locomotive produced in Germany
Technology: The modelled locomotive is a rather modern locomotive. For older locomotives, which are still in operation, aluminium and plastic share may be lower.
Time period: undefined
Production volume: na
Sampling: The data of the material composition and energy consumption is based on oral communication with an expert of one company. 
Extrapolations: Data for one locomotive in operation in Switzerland is used as an estimate for Europe
Uncertainty adjustments: none
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_e9f8c142-1372-38e8-b6fd-28e16d130f90.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
      <geography geographyId="20a9bf48-6cea-59b4-ad08-000cb981f2d0" geographyContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83">
